{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken","id":840066,"title":"Breeds in Forsaken","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-01T11:41:14-08:00","id":840066,"title":"Breeds in Forsaken","content":"I did a thread like this a while back, long before 2e came out; I'd like to try again with 2e in mind. The idea is to port something akin to WtA's Breeds into the metaphysics of WtF. <br /> <br /> First, we probably need a different name than \u201cBreeds\u201d. Unlike WtA and WtF1e, WtF2e doesn't have a hard-and-fast rule that one of your ancestors had to be a Werewolf; all that's required is that you are a Wolf-Blood. And while that <i>usually</i> requires that at least one of your parents was a Wolf-Blood, it's <i>entirely possible</i> for a perfectly ordinary human being to <i>become</i> a Wolf-Blood by being exposed to Lunacy. So the notion of breeding is significantly downplayed, and the uglier aspects of it can be bypassed entirely. So, what to call them if not Breeds? <br /> <br /> Also, let's get this out of the way right now, so it doesn't bog down the rest of the topic: introducing something like Lupus to WtF2e does <i>not</i> require anything <i>remotely</i> like bestiality, unlike WtA; all that's required is to introduce the equivalent notion of Wolf-Blood for wolves. And if you want to firmly slam the door on anything like bestiality, you can reintroduce WtF1e's notion of Ghost Children in cases where such perverse cross-breeding is attempted, and/or add other punishments such as a loss of Renown (e.g., Purity) for attempting such a thing. So please, please, <i>please</i> do not bog this thread down with arguments about how sick you have to be to like the notion of wolf-born Uratha, or intimations about furries being sexual deviants, or any of the other arguments that derailed the original version of this topic. <br /> <br /> With that (hopefully) out of the way: during the spoilers for WtF2e, Stew posted mechanics for Urhanu (Forsaken's equivalent to Lupus) in <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/ephemera-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">this Blog post</a>, which covers the mechanics of the Urhanu in 2e. The only issue I see with this involves Harmony: I don't have my copy hand, so I forget which way \u201cacting like a wolf\u201d Breaks; but if it Breaks toward Spirit, then the Urhanu should probably start with Harmony 4 (the same distance from the middle as 6, but on the spirit/instincts side) or 3 (mirroring man-born Uraha starting at 7). If it breaks toward Flesh, the rules look fine as is. The main thing that would be useful here would be advice on how to get into a wolf's mentality. <br /> <br /> As for Metis equivalents: I could see a place for them in WtF similar to the place held by Banishers in Mage. That is, you get a Metis-equivalent if you botch the First Change. Again, it has nothing to do with breeding; but it <i>does</i> represent a messed-up werewolf. In particular, the Metis-equivalent would not be \u201csomething between human-born and wolf-born\u201d; there would be human-born Metis and there would be wolf-born Metis, since \u201cMetis\u201d has nothing to do with which form you grew up in before tge First Change. Instead, the \u201cMetis Breed\u201d would represent an Uratha who rejected the change, and still considers himself a human or wolf, as the case may be. As such, it might make sense for it to keep Integrity instead of switching over to Harmony. Not that it's likely to keep its Integrity for long\u2026<br /> <br /> (Clarification: by \u201chuman-born\u201d and \u201cwolf-born\u201d, I mean that you were born as, and grew up as, a human or wolf, respectively \u2014 that is, those two \u201cBreeds\u201d represent what your life was like before the First Change. By contrast, the \u201cMetis Breed(s)\u201d would represent a \u201cfail-state\u201d of the First Change itself.)<br /> <br /> This splitting of \u201cMetis\u201d into two \u201cBreeds\u201d also resolves the dilemma brought about by the temporary nature of the Gauru form: there are no \u201cBreeds\u201d associated with that form. Instead, \u201chuman-born Metis\u201d would default to the wolfman form, while \u201cwolf-born Metis\u201d would default to the \u201cdire wolf\u201d form. <br /> <br /> So: four \u201cBreeds\u201d, corresponding to four of the five forms a werewolf can take. Two of them represent normal werewolves, two represent twisted werewolves; two of them represent werewolves who grew up as humans, two of them represent werewolves that grew up as wolves. <br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:05:29-08:00","id":840080,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure you don't have to be wolf-blooded to go through the First Change, as a note.<br /> <br /> I think one of the difficulties here will be making characters who are quite literally wolves into people. It seems like the First Change loses some of it's <i>Chronicles of Darkness</i> specific pathos if the most traumatic thing your First Change did was change the social conventions for sniffing butts.<br /> <br /> Does the Translation Guide include any lore worth discussing for the Urhanu?<br /> <br /> Also, shouldn't one just avoid the &quot;metis&quot; term entirely, since that seemed to be the source of so many arguments over the concept itself?<br /> <br /> I'm having a hard time understanding the need for the metis ones when having the human born and the wolf born seem to be the only ones that make sense.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I'm pretty sure the state of being Uratha is largely apathetic to your feelings about it, so I can't see why them trying to be just a human or a wolf would make them keep Integrity. In fact, that seems to be the exact sort of thing that high Harmony describes, because either way the wolf and the human (in this case? sort of? I still think it breaks down a bit here) are still of the Flesh.<br /> <br /> EDIT: To be clear, I'm not knocking on the premise of the Urhanu, I'd just like to hear more about them. I am however knocking on the need for the metis breeds, calling them metis breeds, and the notion that the First Change gives one whit about how you feel about being a werewolf. (Otherwise, if it was just about rejecting your heritage, how would <i>American </i><i>Werewolf in London </i>Ghost Wolves happen like described in the book? Again, isn't what they're doing indicative of just plain old high Harmony?<br /> <br /> Or put another way, does it need the mechanical change when it already fits within the auspice of the base mechanics?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 03-01-2016, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:05:39-08:00","id":840081,"title":"","content":"I have thoughts. I will return to this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:20:40-08:00","id":840091,"title":"","content":"Like I wrote in the original thread, human and wolf born make sense. Metis do not, because Uratha just aren't as tightly knit culture to really show the essence of the breed. And Forsaken in general is about duality of man and wolf, metis have no place in the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T12:47:33-08:00","id":840111,"title":"","content":"Quick note: I've been putting in quotes terms that I'm borrowing from WtA for lack of anything better. I've already asked for alternative suggestions to replace \u201cBreed\u201d; extending that, I have no intention of actually using the term \u201cMetis\u201d \u2014 I just don't have anything else that conveys the notion I'm going for \u2014 not that \u201cMetis\u201d conveys it all that well, either. <br /> <br /> As well, I'm not convinced that the concept of wolfman/dire wolf \u201cBreeds\u201d is workable \u2014 but neither am I convinced that they're fundamentally a bad idea, either. What I'm thinking is that the \u201cBreeds\u201d correspond more or less to self-identification: not the extreme version that you get when wildly out of Harmony, but a more moderate sense of \u201cI tend to think of myself as human\u201d or \u201cI tend to think of myself as a wolf\u201d. In that regard, the wolfman and dire wolf \u201cBreeds\u201d would be \u201cI tend to think of myself as a monstrous human\u201d and \u201cI tend to think of myself as a monstrous wolf\u201d, respectively \u2014 and a particularly ugly First Change would be a likely reason for a new Uratha to think of itself as monstrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T16:07:14-08:00","id":840229,"title":"","content":"What if &quot;Breeds&quot; were something entirely different from &quot;Born-Man or Born-Wolf&quot;? What if some werewolves were stronger, some had more stamina, and others had deformities and flaws (like a Metis)? All those changes could be justified by some specific Hisil conditions that plague different places on earth. Uratha whose first change happens in the Amazon forest acquire dark-red patches of fur, bigger ears and specialized claws to climb trees. Werewolves of the Sahara Desert could have an easier time withstanding heat and handling lack of water, with increased stamina and fur to blend with the sands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5446-binaly","name":"BinAly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"146"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T16:21:31-08:00","id":840237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BinAly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840229#post840229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if &quot;Breeds&quot; were something entirely different from &quot;Born-Man or Born-Wolf&quot;? What if some werewolves were stronger, some had more stamina, and others had deformities and flaws (like a Metis)? All those changes could be justified by some specific Hisil conditions that plague different places on earth. Uratha whose first change happens in the Amazon forest acquire dark-red patches of fur, bigger ears and specialized claws to climb trees. Werewolves of the Sahara Desert could have an easier time withstanding heat and handling lack of water, with increased stamina and fur to blend with the sands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would they all be born human, though? I think the issue with breeds is basically that, can you play an uratha not born human?<br /> <br /> As for your suggestion, in the first corebook, there is an African Wilddog Iron Master. And one Lodges book focuses on what forms african uratha take. Hyena was one, hilariously enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T16:43:38-08:00","id":840249,"title":"","content":"As Ana points out, \u201cBreeds\u201d aren't intended to represent mere attribute biases and/or conditions. I've got quotes around \u201cBreed\u201d because it's <i>not</i> intended to be \u201cwhat type of wolf is my wolf-form?\u201d which can reasonably be handled by shifting an attribute or skill dot around; it's specifically supposed to be along the lines of \u201cborn and raised as a human\u201d or \u201cborn and raised as a wolf\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:12:30-08:00","id":840268,"title":"","content":"What's the point of playing a character born and raised as a wolf?<br /> <br /> I could see it in Apocalypse, where actual wolves were a large part of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:15:49-08:00","id":840273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840268#post840268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the point of playing a character born and raised as a wolf?<br /> <br /> I could see it in Apocalypse, where actual wolves were a large part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://www.angelfire.com/rpg2/red_talon/lupusguide.html\" target=\"_blank\">For example.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:29:54-08:00","id":840277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840268#post840268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the point of playing a character born and raised as a wolf?<br /> <br /> I could see it in Apocalypse, where actual wolves were a large part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>(Sadly, most Apoc games involve wolves rarely XD )<br /> <br /> The idea how it would go, mostly. How would it make the uratha different, when they lean closer to the wild than human,etc.<br /> <br /> Also, Ephsy, that guide is pretty old. Even WtA's take on lupus has changed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:37:36-08:00","id":840280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840277#post840277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea how it would go, mostly. How would it make the uratha different, when they lean closer to the wild than human,etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I'm trying to figure out, though. Werewolves are torn between the flesh and the spirit. The wolf has little to do with it beyond symbolism.<br /> <br /> What is a werewolf born and raised as a wolf going to do in a game, beyond being awful at socializing with humans and not get the representations of spirits?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:41:19-08:00","id":840281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840280#post840280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's what I'm trying to figure out, though. Werewolves are torn between the flesh and the spirit. The wolf has little to do with it beyond symbolism.<br /> <br /> What is a werewolf born and raised as a wolf going to do in a game, beyond being awful at socializing with humans and not get the representations of spirits?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I admit you are correct in that part. At least in 2nd ed, the wolf is much less part of the game outside how uratha act.<br /> <br /> Could the alternative be spirit-born, then?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T17:44:45-08:00","id":840283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840281#post840281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could the alternative be spirit-born, then?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is something like that in Skinchangers. I think it's name is Scavenger Wolf, or Dog, or Coyote. It was a spirit that envied werewolves and wanted to shift like they did, so it learned how. I guess you could have a spirit of the hunt that sort of awakens as a living flesh creature. Most probably wouldn't survive, if their first change was in the Hisil and they passed out there where other spirits would just eat them up, but you would have a different viewpoint that would make more sense for the game, one being from the spirit world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T19:50:00-08:00","id":840341,"title":"","content":"I feel like I've been down this particular sidetrack before\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840268#post840268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's the point of playing a character born and raised as a wolf?</div> </div> </div> </div>A fun roleplaying experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840268#post840268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could see it in Apocalypse, where actual wolves were a large part of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but there are a large number of unrelated reasons why I'd rather play WtF than WtA. So I'd rather do the comparatively minor hacks needed to tweak WtF to better support wolves than the near-complete overhauls that I'd need to apply to WtA to get it the way I want it \u2014 especially since the end result of those overhauls would more closely resemble WtF than WtA anyway. <br /> <br /> In a game that features wolf-born, the role of wolves in the game would be expanded. At the very least, you'd have the aforementioned wolfish counterparts to wolf-blood humans. In WtF as written, there's a box talking about how the Pure sometimes include wolves as part of their Packs; in a game with wolf-born werewolves, that wouldn't be restricted to the Pure. Indeed, wolves would likely be a staple of <i>most</i> Packs, with a \u201cPack without wolves\u201d being the exception rather than the rule. <br /> <br /> And finally, these wouldn't be real-world wolves; even the ones that <i>aren't</i> counterparts to wolf-blood humans wouod be more akin to Mowgli's brothers from Rudyard Kipling's <b>Jungle Book</b>, just with a darker, more savage flavor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T20:06:20-08:00","id":840349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840341#post840341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In WtF as written, there's a box talking about how the Pure sometimes include wolves as part of their Packs; in a game with wolf-born werewolves, that wouldn't be restricted to the Pure. Indeed, wolves would likely be a staple of <i>most</i> Packs, with a \u201cPack without wolves\u201d being the exception rather than the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two things. One, it's not restricted to the Pure, every werewolf has access to the Wolf Gifts that let them speak with animals and the ability to bring them into the pack, it's just more common among Predator Kings because they tend to live in the wilds. Which leads to the second point. Wolves are pretty rare, there's supposed to be about 200,000 in the entire world, that's less than the populations of vampires and werewolves in first edition. With none in South or Central America, Africa, or Australia outside of zoos. Even in North America they're uncommon and nonexistent in many places. Even if they are supernaturally gifted wolves, they're going to limit your playing areas.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying don't do it or anything but as someone who doesn't understand <i>why</i>, I'd like to know what it's all about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T20:21:41-08:00","id":840351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840277#post840277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> (Sadly, most Apoc games involve wolves rarely XD )<br /> <br /> The idea how it would go, mostly. How would it make the uratha different, when they lean closer to the wild than human,etc.<br /> <br /> Also, Ephsy, that guide is pretty old. Even WtA's take on lupus has changed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I couldn't find the one Mark Reig Hagen typed up for Red Talons Revised edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T20:26:08-08:00","id":840354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840351#post840351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I couldn't find the one Mark Reig Hagen typed up for Red Talons Revised edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, Red Talons do not stand for all of wolfborn. They are basically what Glass Walkers are to homid garou. Extreme version to one side of the duality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T20:37:22-08:00","id":840362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840354#post840354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, Red Talons do not stand for all of wolfborn. They are basically what Glass Walkers are to homid garou. Extreme version to one side of the duality.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, the text was about portraying lupus, not portraying Red Talons. It was included there because it's the sensible place in which to include it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T21:21:14-08:00","id":840378,"title":"","content":"It was Scavenger Wolf, though he wasn't a Firstborn or anything. He did a sort of reverse skin-thieving thing, pretty neat background. I find myself warming to the idea of spirit-turned-werewolf. There's a drastic change of sensibilities, but also loss. You've left the predatory world of the Hisil to the life of a person, providing you don't lean heavily towards Low Harmony. Plus you lose your immortality. Most spirits probably don't get to thinking about how nice it is to be an ageless ephemeral. Huge change, that, especially once you're human enough to realize it.<br /> <br /> Anyways, like I said, I don't get it but I always like seeing what people do with the game. Hope the thread goes well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T22:19:40-08:00","id":840411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840349#post840349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying don't do it or anything but as someone who doesn't understand <i>why</i>, I'd like to know what it's all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can only speak for myself, but I just enjoy the symmetry. If certain people sometimes gain the ability to turn into wolves, why shouldn't certain wolves sometimes gain the ability to turn into people? Duality is a pretty significant recurring theme with werewolves, so it feels a little like a lose end for the progression to always go human &gt; wolf and never wolf &gt; human. For all the talk of &quot;Uratha don't have a 'true form', they have five&quot; it sure seems like Hishu is their true form, since they all spend the first dozen and change years of their lives without access to any of the other four forms. If some of them spent those early years in Hishu and others spent them in Urhan, it would feel a lot more... I don't know, complete? That's not the right word but I'm at a loss at the moment. <br /> <br /> I guess it mostly just comes down to &quot;I think it's cool.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T23:07:15-08:00","id":840432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840378#post840378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was Scavenger Wolf, though he wasn't a Firstborn or anything. He did a sort of reverse skin-thieving thing, pretty neat background. I find myself warming to the idea of spirit-turned-werewolf. There's a drastic change of sensibilities, but also loss. You've left the predatory world of the Hisil to the life of a person, providing you don't lean heavily towards Low Harmony. Plus you lose your immortality. Most spirits probably don't get to thinking about how nice it is to be an ageless ephemeral. Huge change, that, especially once you're human enough to realize it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could see <i>that</i> being WtF's Metis counterpart: neither human nor wolf, and a natural shapeshifter. If you keep the idea of this \u201cBreed\u201d having a physical deformity, you might associate the latter with whatever the spirits Ban was. <br /> <br /> Regardless, I wouldn't do this <i>instead of</i> the Urhanu \u201cBreed\u201d; if I'd do it at all, it would be <i>in addition to</i> Urhanu \u2014 and it would be the rarest of the three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-01T23:17:46-08:00","id":840439,"title":"","content":"So, my opinion on this matter: I've always liked the idea of Lupus/Urhanu, but I've always found the execution unsatisfying. Not to knock Stu's 2e Urhanu conversion, it's definitely a viable way to do it, but it's not the way I would do it.<br /> <br /> I would start with the form bonuses. It's weird to me that a character born as a wolf would have +2 dexterity and +1 stamina all the time in the form they were born in. I would re-do the form bonuses for Urhanu so that Urhan is their baseline from which the other forms add bonuses and penalties, just like for human-born werewolves Hishu is the baseline.<br /> <br /> Next, I would look at Harmony. Harmony isn't human at one end and wolf at the other, so starting Urhanu at lower harmony than human-born werewolves doesn't make a lot of sense to me. Harmony is flesh at one end and spirit at the other. So what I would do there is re-do Harmony Breaking Points for Urhanu. Human-born werewolves experience Breaking Points towards flesh when they act like a human and Breaking Points towards spirit when they act like a spirit. Acting like a wolf doesn't really enter into the equation. So, for Urhanu I would leave Breaking Points towards spirit the same, but change Breaking Points towards flesh so they experience them for acting like a wolf.<br /> <br /> Finally, I would look at Tells. I agree wholeheartedly with Dataweaver that the way to go with Urhanu is to make a wolf equivalent of Wolf-Blooded humans. Personally, I think Were-Blooded would be a really cool name for them. But a lot of Wolf-Blooded Tells wouldn't work very well for Were-Blooded, so I'd make some new ones that fit closer better with wolf-born characters.<br /> <br /> And that's it. I'd avoid any further changes like giving Urhanu limits or penalties on mental Skills or bonuses on Reaching, because to me that makes them feel less like Uratha that just came at it from the opposite end of the human/wolf spectrum and more like a whole different kind of werewolf.<br /> <br /> That's my take on it, anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-02-2016, 02:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T00:43:10-08:00","id":840473,"title":"","content":"So, a few things.<br /> <br /> First off, Ancestry is a good replacement for Breed, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Secondly, verifying an idea, for an Urhanu, acting like a wolf is a break towards the Flesh. They should start at Harmony 7, as anyone else. Keep The mental stigmas. I'm fairly cool with them having greater resonance with the spirit border, but I also dig sharpening some of their senses (as if a werewolf needed sharper senses, I know).<br /> <br /> Your ideas for the Ulle'u (Forsaken Metis) are best captured by the extremist endings of Flesh or Spirit and are better left to that. I would keep the Ulle'u more or less as is, except I'd get rid of the acting breaking points and instead tighten up the time schedules for being one or the other, while offering some bonus to shifting.<br /> <br /> So, all this said and done, why, beyond the cool factor?<br /> <br /> Well, because both games talk about ecosystem. Apocalypse was more about how we disrupt the ecosystem of areas, but Forsaken is about being a part of it. Forsaken they may be, but in as much as there are natural orders in this Sundered World<sup>TM</sup>, the Uratha are part of it. The thing of the matter is, with the different Ancestries, we all have our own biases and perspectives that we need to move away from. The Hishu Ancestry allows new players to be the outsiders looking in on the Forsaken life and the world of the spirits, while the Ulle'u allow people more comfortable and experienced with it to provide the outsider view of normal humanity's view of this ecosystem. It's playing Forsaken in different ways.<br /> <br /> So, what about the Urhanu? Well, ostensibly, it allows us an opportunity to challenge our norms and then bring our findings in conflict with other people at the table. The Urhanu is removed from the cycle that the Hishu and Ulle'u can argue around in, and therefore can intellectually and spiritually challenge and stimulate the other players.<br /> <br /> The trio of Ancestries allow for different dialogues in relation to Forsaken's ideas and themes-to be part of a larger cycle of (super)nature while most of that cycle seeks to shove them out. To be the outsider on the inside, in many ways.<br /> <br /> Not a whole lot more to say.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T08:44:56-08:00","id":840684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840473#post840473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep The mental stigmas. I'm fairly cool with them having greater resonance with the spirit border, but I also dig sharpening some of their senses (as if a werewolf needed sharper senses, I know).</div> </div> </div> </div>I can kind of get the limitations on mental Skills just because they aren't educated the same ways humans are. But I still don't like it. If human-born Uratha gain the instincts of a wolf, why wouldn't Urhanu gain the conscious reasoning of a human? Sure, they haven't spent their early years in a school, but let's not limit character backgrounds by saying that automatically means they can't take mental Skills as primary. What about the Urhanu who became fascinated with human academia and spent years studying after their First Change so they could eventually take the GED and try to get into a human college?<br /> <br /> The greater ease of Reaching I just don't understand, especially if you're establishing that for Urhanu, being a wolf is as much a part of the flesh as being a human is for human-born. If being a wolf doesn't bring them closer to the spirit side of things (which I agree it shouldn't), why would they have an easier time crossing between spirit and flesh? I'm not necessarily opposed to the idea, I just can't see any impetus for it.<br /> <br /> Further sharpened senses I'm definitely opposed to. Human-born Uratha already have wolf senses. Why would an Urhanu's wolf senses be stronger than a human-born's wolf senses? They're both the senses of a wolf. Are Urhanu's human senses weaker than human-born's too? Why or why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-02-2016, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:36:25-08:00","id":840717,"title":"","content":"The ease with which they breach the gauntlet almost seems to be an Apocalypse throwback, where Lupus were naturally better at crossing because it went off Gnosis and they got the most at chargen by default. Doesn't make quite so much sense here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:42:30-08:00","id":840720,"title":"","content":"I could see that Urhanu just use their Urhan Attributes as base - and maybe go from other side of Harmony, on level 3. I would also do not limit them on Mental Skills. Maybe give them a bit better senses but make them a bit more fragile? Or make them more pack-dependent than even Hishu Uratha?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T09:42:49-08:00","id":840721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=840717#post840717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ease with which they breach the gauntlet almost seems to be an Apocalypse throwback, where Lupus were naturally better at crossing because it went off Gnosis and they got the most at chargen by default. Doesn't make quite so much sense here.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would explain why it was lost on me. Seems like something that would be better off going the way of Klaives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-02T10:48:22-08:00","id":840770,"title":"","content":"I think the problem here is you lot are relying too heavily on the flesh. So the wolf aspect of the uratha is mostly symbolic, aye? Then perhaps this &quot;wolf&quot; breed is of the first borns children? I see no reason why that's cant work. Fenris-ur has a child with x spirit and for some random ass reason it can also be of shifter stock. He is of father wolfs blood after all. <br /> <br /> Y'all keep saying duality and mentioning the hisil, I'm surprised this hasn't come up before (far as I can tell). Never mind that this eliminates a large portion of the lupus issues (intellect, beastiality blah blah blah).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:34:43-07:00","id":848781,"title":"","content":"I notice we keep coming back to this... was this such a great mechanic in WTA? Not that I dislike the idea, but out of all the werewolf concepts, this comes up almost as often as the hot Uratha love making threads before the devs said werewolves could lay the pipe without worrying about evil wolf spawn. It always surprises me XD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T07:53:26-07:00","id":848790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848781#post848781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I notice we keep coming back to this... was this such a great mechanic in WTA? Not that I dislike the idea, but out of all the werewolf concepts, this comes up almost as often as the hot Uratha love making threads before the devs said werewolves could lay the pipe without worrying about evil wolf spawn. It always surprises me XD.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I explained earlier, for me it's about symmetry. Werewolf has a big duality theme going on, and it seems like if there are people with wolf-like instinct who gain the ability to turn into wolves, why shouldn't there be wolves with human-like intellect who gain the ability to turn into humans?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T08:14:18-07:00","id":848803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848790#post848790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As I explained earlier, for me it's about symmetry. Werewolf has a big duality theme going on, and it seems like if there are people with wolf-like instinct who gain the ability to turn into wolves, why shouldn't there be wolves with human-like intellect who gain the ability to turn into humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>&lt;shrug&gt; Because is destroys a common premise with all the supernatural lines - that they are more human than not, as seen by everything being a template layered on top of a baseline human? It kinda also undermines relatability - we know what humans feel, but don't really know what a wolf would be like before the First Change?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:23:33-07:00","id":848831,"title":"","content":"Don't like it, don't use it. It's optional rules for fans of manwolves. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:31:31-07:00","id":848834,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848781#post848781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I notice we keep coming back to this... was this such a great mechanic in WTA? Not that I dislike the idea, but out of all the werewolf concepts, this comes up almost as often as the hot Uratha love making threads before the devs said werewolves could lay the pipe without worrying about evil wolf spawn. It always surprises me XD.</div> </div> </div> </div>In WtA, it was a direct way for players to comment on the environmentalist themes of the game and reinforced the sense of Gaia fighting back. It was pretty damn relevant for everything Apocalypse was trying to do.<br /> <br /> Forsaken has less of a precedent in regards to the things it says, and the Urhanu have less to say here than they do in Apocalypse. That's not say they can't serve a purpose, but the dialogue does not inherently need a chorus for the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T09:37:48-07:00","id":848841,"title":"","content":"Question: How about approaching the Spirit-Flesh hybrid angle from the other way? A wolf or hunting spirit that gains corporeal form, developing from a relatively simple spirit into a complex quasicorporeal entity? Would this be an appropriate equivalent of the wolf breed in the Forsaken context?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/607039-homebrew-mechs-walkers-ect\" target=\"_blank\">Mechs:</a> Because even the Chronicles of Darkness needs robot fights.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/813387-darkframe-a-far-future-crossover-setting\" target=\"_blank\">DarkFrame</a>: Crossover setting that puts Chronicles of Darkness in the far future that is Warframe.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/760136-monarch-the-endless\" target=\"_blank\">Monarch: The Endless</a> You are an alien ruler, charged with maintaining a people who you shape to suit your needs.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7015-almarck","name":"Almarck","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:32:55-07:00","id":848862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848841#post848841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: How about approaching the Spirit-Flesh hybrid angle from the other way? A wolf or hunting spirit that gains corporeal form, developing from a relatively simple spirit into a complex quasicorporeal entity? Would this be an appropriate equivalent of the wolf breed in the Forsaken context?</div> </div> </div> </div>That has actually been discussed in this thread. And it's definitely not a bad idea. For me personally, it's not what I want in Forsaken equivalent of Breeds, but I do see the appeal it has for others.<br /> <br /> The thing is, for me, Uratha aren't spirits. They're Pangeans. So to me it doesn't make a lot of sense for them to be born as ephemeral entities, because Pangeans aren't ephemeral. However, as the book states, werewolves don't have a true form, they have five true forms (all of which are material). If that's the case, why would they only ever be born in Hishu form? I would think it would make more sense for some be born in Hishu form to human parents and some be born in Urhan form to wolf parents. It would make sense for some to be born in the hybrid forms too, if there were anything in the natural world that resembled those forms to serve as parents. I like to imagine that before the Sundering, some of them might have been born in hybrid forms to Pangean patents. Maybe the first pack was born in Gauru; after all, it's said that was the Father's form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-17-2016, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T10:33:07-07:00","id":848864,"title":"","content":"Having played a 'spirit' for the majority of one game, let me just say that it's both harder than most players might think on when doing it constantly, and that it also makes some of the innate empathy harder.<br /> <br /> Not an impossible angle, but the Flesh is familiar, and it makes more sense to start from there than the Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:32:20-07:00","id":848901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848803#post848803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;shrug&gt; Because is destroys a common premise with all the supernatural lines - that they are more human than not, as seen by everything being a template layered on top of a baseline human?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree with that premise. Vampire is all about slowly becoming not-human. Prometheans were created as something fundamentally inhuman and strive to become human. Demons are completely alien and only use humanity as a cover to hide from the God-Machine. Lots of splats are more inhuman than not, and in my opinion, werewolves are among those splats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848803#post848803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It kinda also undermines relatability - we know what humans feel, but don't really know what a wolf would be like before the First Change?</div> </div> </div> </div>My first response to that is it doesn't have to be. If werewolves born in Hishu form have wolf-like instincts, it makes sense for Urhanu to have human-like intellect. The character can be just as relatable as any werewolf, even if their situation is not. My second response is, isn't that the point of roleplaying? Expanding our experiences by empathizing with characters who have different experiences and different worldviews than we do? I may not know exactly how it feels to be the only pup in my litter with the self-awareness and critical thinking skills of a human, but I can empathize with the feeling of not fitting in because my mind works differently than others' minds, and I can extrapolate from that feeling to portray a character with sincerity. My third response is, I don't think Urhanu need to be a core feature in Forsaken. I fully understand that they're a departure from the default setting. But they're a departure I think is cool, so I'm interested in discussing it. As Wyrdhampster said, if you don't like it, no one is going to make you use it in your games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:37:32-07:00","id":848904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848901#post848901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't agree with that premise. Vampire is all about slowly becoming not-human. Prometheans were created as something fundamentally inhuman and strive to become human. Demons are completely alien and only use humanity as a cover to hide from the God-Machine. Lots of splats are more inhuman than not, and in my opinion, werewolves are among those splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree: Humanity is the whole premise of Promethean. Vampires cling to it desperately, and the whole reason a demon fell is because it, consciously or not, choose humanity over servitude. Every catalyst is a fundamentally human choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:49:48-07:00","id":848907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848904#post848904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree: Humanity is the whole premise of Promethean. Vampires cling to it desperately, and the whole reason a demon fell is because it, consciously or not, choose humanity over servitude. Every catalyst is a fundamentally human choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, that's fine. Doesn't change the fact that a lot of folks like the idea of Urhanu. If you don't like the idea of Urhanu, and you're just in this thread to talk about why they shouldn't be a thing, all you're doing is threadcrapping.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T11:57:34-07:00","id":848908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848901#post848901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying don't. You asked for possible reasons and I responded with what I could come up with. I don't actually care either way.<br /> <br /> Some other ones (of varying merit):<br /> <br /> It doesn't fit the lore? Specifically regarding the &quot;Shall Cleave to the Human&quot; part of the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> It isn't needed? It doesn't really fill a role in the narrative, as pointed out, so why bother adding it? Obviously, this isn't persuasive, because you <i>do</i> want to play such a character, so the effort <i>is</i> warranted.<br /> <br /> Such a character would have disproportionately more difficulty in adapting? They wouldn't have any reason to acquire human Skills or many Mental/Social Merits pre-First Change.<br /> <br /> Summary: Some things to consider. They all have a number of answers to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":".  Thought of more reasons. 03-17-2016, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:32:02-07:00","id":848918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848907#post848907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, that's fine. Doesn't change the fact that a lot of folks like the idea of Urhanu. If you don't like the idea of Urhanu, and you're just in this thread to talk about why they shouldn't be a thing, all you're doing is threadcrapping.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did none of those things. I, in fact, loved playing characters that aren't androcentric in Apocalypse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:40:22-07:00","id":848922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Almarck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848841#post848841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: How about approaching the Spirit-Flesh hybrid angle from the other way? A wolf or hunting spirit that gains corporeal form, developing from a relatively simple spirit into a complex quasicorporeal entity? Would this be an appropriate equivalent of the wolf breed in the Forsaken context?</div> </div> </div> </div>As I mentioned earlier, I think \u201cspirit-born\u201d might work as the explanation for a WtF counterpart to the Metis: not of man, nor of wolf. (What does \u201cUlle'u\u201d mean, anyway? We might need to rename it in light of this reinterpretation.) I wouldn't want to replace the wolf-born with the spirit-born; but I could see having both. <br /> <br /> In fact, how about this: in WtA, the Homid and Lupus Breeds were presented as polar opposites, with the Metis existing in a middle ground between them; but in the context of WtF, I could see the Urhanu and the Ulle'u being \u201coff-center\u201d, with the Urhanu having a special affinity for Father Wolf and the Ulle'u having a similar affinity with Mother Luna. Meanwhile, the <i>Hishu</i> would occupy the \u201cmiddle ground\u201d, having a natural affinity for balance between the flesh and the spirit. Some possible manifestations of this arrangement: the Ulle'u might have some sort of edge when it comes to Shadow Gifts, while the Urhanu get a similar edge with respect to Wolf Gifts; the Ulle'u might get some sort of bias toward Breaking toward Spirit while the Urhanu get a bias toward Breaking toward Flesh. (The Ulle'u \u201cdeformities\u201d thing can go, as far as I'm concerned; if it's kept, it should be representative of what sort of spirit you were before your encounter with Mother Luna.)<br /> <br /> The Pure Tribes probably have \u201cBreed\u201d preferences, with the Fire-Touched tending to recruit from Ulle'u, the Predator Kings recruiting from the Urhanu, and the Ivory Claws favoring the Hishu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:43:49-07:00","id":848924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848908#post848908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not saying don't. You asked for possible reasons and I responded with what I could come up with. I don't actually care either way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. My fault for phrasing the reasoning for my like of the concept in the form of a rhetorical question. I didn't really want an answer, I was using it as a way to illustrate my line of thinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848908#post848908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some other ones (of varying merit):<br /> <br /> It doesn't fit the lore? Specifically regarding the &amp;quot;Shall Cleave to the Human&amp;quot; part of the Oath of the Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see how Urhanu violate that part of the oath. Just because were-blooded are born of lupine parents doesn't in any way prevent Urhanu from cleaving to humanity. It might be more of a challenge for them than it would for a human-born werewolves, but I see that as a fun roleplaying opportunity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848908#post848908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't needed? It doesn't really fill a role in the narrative, as pointed out, so why bother adding it? Obviously, this isn't persuasive, because you <i>do</i> want to play such a character, so the effort <i>is</i> warranted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it does fill a role in the narrative; as I said, it helps illustrate that werewolves aren't just humans with shape shifting powers, they're shapeshifters capable of taking human (as well as other) forms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848908#post848908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Such a character would have disproportionately more difficulty in adapting? They wouldn't have any reason to acquire human Skills or many Mental/Social Merits pre-First Change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Difficulty in adapting I see as part of the appeal of the concept. It's a roleplaying challenge, just like playing a character with a Persistent Condition. And I disagree that they wouldn't have any reason to pick up human skills pre-first change. Lots of humans learn survival skills. A wolf with human intellect would surely be driven to seek out more mentally and socially stimulating experiences than they would easily find in a pack of mundane wolves. They might not learn Drive or Computer pre-first change, but I could certainly see them learning others. And ultimately, I would prefer to leave those kinds of background choices up to the player.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848908#post848908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Summary: Some things to consider. They all have a number of answers to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I'm not interested in considering why *not* to play Urhanu. I'm more interested in considering how to fit them into Forsaken.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:47:20-07:00","id":848928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848918#post848918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did none of those things. I, in fact, loved playing characters that aren't androcentric in Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I wasn't referring to you specifically. I meant, in general the trend of folks coming to the thread asking why this idea keeps coming up, and then proceeding to argue against the reasons people give for liking the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:49:37-07:00","id":848930,"title":"","content":"Why would a wolf born or spirit born Uratha have any investment in keeping both worlds separated? Spirits have a lot to gain from bypassing the restriction, after all. It's something that fits more the Pure mindset.<br /> <br /> &quot;Homid&quot; Uratha do it out of pragmatism. The spirit lorded hellish realms presided by shadow deities that threatened all of Pangaea are enough of a cautionary tale.<br /> <br /> Would spirit born Uratha, literal children and grandchildren of the firstborn be so compelled by ban?<br /> <br /> What about Urhanu? Instinct?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T12:55:51-07:00","id":848933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848930#post848930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a wolf born or spirit born Uratha have any investment in keeping both worlds separated? Spirits have a lot to gain from bypassing the restriction, after all. It's something that fits more the Pure mindset.<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;Homid&amp;quot; Uratha do it out of pragmatism. The spirit lorded hellish realms presided by shadow deities that threatened all of Pangaea are enough of a cautionary tale.<br /> <br /> Would spirit born Uratha, literal children and grandchildren of the firstborn be so compelled by ban?<br /> <br /> What about Urhanu? Instinct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, a wolf is just as much a creature of flesh as a human is, so for Urhanu, the reason is the same as it is for human-born werewolves. It suits the needs of their territory. I still don't really care for the idea of spirit-born Uratha, but Dataweaver seemed to imply that they'd have a preference within the Pure Tribes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:03:30-07:00","id":848939,"title":"","content":"The notion of the spirit-born Uratha is by far the most problematic of the three, and the one most in need of development before it's usable; I'm not entirely comfortable with them as they stand. For instance, where did its flesh come from? We're not talking about Claiming here; but we <i>are</i> talking about something that started out as spirit and now is a melding of flesh and spirit. And yeah, there's also the question of why a spirit-born Uratha would want to keep the two worlds apart.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T13:08:45-07:00","id":848942,"title":"","content":"Presumably as it is now a werewolf it is also now not a spirit. It cannot be a part of a choir, it cannot survive solely on Essence that leaks through the Gauntlet. Spirits will be hostile to it in a way that even magath aren't treated.<br /> <br /> For a spirit-turned-werewolf, the Oath of the Moon is an instruction guide for how to live now that you've been separated from everything you've ever known.<br /> <br /> I do believe they'd lean more towards the Fire-Touched than anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T15:16:53-07:00","id":849007,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=848834#post848834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In WtA, it was a direct way for players to comment on the environmentalist themes of the game and reinforced the sense of Gaia fighting back. It was pretty damn relevant for everything Apocalypse was trying to do.<br /> <br /> Forsaken has less of a precedent in regards to the things it says, and the Urhanu have less to say here than they do in Apocalypse. That's not say they can't serve a purpose, but the dialogue does not inherently need a chorus for the world.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose so, though I always found the breeds to be an incredibly ham-fisted approach to those theme in WTA... it lacked the nuance that I felt would of worked better. Then again, WTA wasn't really a game about Nuance with it's themes, it was more &quot;HUMANS ARE SHITBAGS THAT ONLY EMPOWER THE WYRM OR WEAVER, KILL EM ALL! CAUSE CAPTAIN PLAN- I MEAN GAEA NEEDS US TO PURGE THE UNCLEAN. CAUSE LOOTING AND POLLUTING IS NOT THE WAY YOU BASTARDS&quot;.... at least as it got closer and closer to the time of judgment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T16:39:32-07:00","id":849034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849007#post849007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose so, though I always found the breeds to be an incredibly ham-fisted approach to those theme in WTA... it lacked the nuance that I felt would of worked better. Then again, WTA wasn't really a game about Nuance with it's themes, it was more &quot;HUMANS ARE SHITBAGS THAT ONLY EMPOWER THE WYRM OR WEAVER, KILL EM ALL! CAUSE CAPTAIN PLAN- I MEAN GAEA NEEDS US TO PURGE THE UNCLEAN. CAUSE LOOTING AND POLLUTING IS NOT THE WAY YOU BASTARDS&quot;.... at least as it got closer and closer to the time of judgment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Alright, now the above is threadcrapping.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T17:13:43-07:00","id":849044,"title":"","content":"I would just wind up using wolf born uratha to do Jungle Book, Chronicles of Darkness edition, among other somewhat goofy ideas.<br /> <br /> Also, I like the idea of an urhanu born into a captive wolf pack in a zoo that somehow managed to induct it's zookeepers into the uratha pack it joined, thus flipping the relationship between them.<br /> <br /> And of course, there is the urhanu that somehow managed to gain a powerful position in human society, despite the fact that it is faking it's credentials, but is good at the job anyway.. for best result, make it a position where that old saying about business people, psychopaths and predatory animals can be a central theme and then throw in some blatant lies by the urhanu as to their credentials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T18:36:17-07:00","id":849063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849034#post849034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alright, now the above is threadcrapping.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. Probably.<br /> <br /> But I don't think anyone can deny Apocalypse was a blunt game, in ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T19:07:56-07:00","id":849076,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Let's try to get back to the topic, here. This thread is about what would need to be done to incorporate the concept of Breeds into Forsaken. Arguing why Breeds shouldn't be in Forsaken or why you didn't like them in Apocalypse are off-topic.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T19:28:37-07:00","id":849078,"title":"","content":"I feel like that design space is unnecessary. There's only so much that you can do or that it offers that isn't already represented in the game. I mean, being a born and raised Predator King basically covers 90% of the roleplaying opportunities that a Metis equivalent would. You'd be feral and potentially unfamiliar with the trappings of human society (with pack kin and two wolves and everything). I played a game with a character who turned Urhan after her first change and couldn't figure out how to change back. Basically lived in the woods with wolves for 4 years, forgetting what she was. That could easily be altered to be a Second Skin Wolfblood who couldn't figure out the shedding process. The advantage being that you can play unfamiliar, but moderate it as you please. You're not completely off the grid of relatability.<br /> <br /> As far as it being an actual wolf who suddenly gets the ability to become human, so much is lost in that process and it offers very little that isn't sort of dead horse material at this point. Even the aforementioned examples I used I think have to be handled with care. Most of it would be tiring for both the player and the people he plays with. A lot of the roleplaying a wolfbreed promotes is very uninspired or tired stuff in my opinion. The mute. The broken language user. The anti-social/socially inept one. The one who solves all his problems through violence. The lone wolf. The simple one. The one who doesn't get sarcasm. It sounds fun in theory, but I think it generally plays out otherwise. Anytime someone played a newly changed werewolf and I had to explain what spirits are in-game, it's always felt more like a chore than actual resonant roleplay. Multiply that a couple times over for a wolfborn.<br /> <br /> Not that anything done with werewolves is ever truly original, but I think all those traits I just mentioned are actually more hindrances to good roleplay than actual opportunities. Especially if you get more than one of those traits in a single character. The only thing you get in the trade-off is more in touch with your wolfside, which you frankly just don't need a wolf-origin for. Just play a character who feels more comfortable with his wolf-skin. Get an extra dot of primal urge and get Favored Form: Urhan and you did it, baby.<br /> <br /> As far as relatability: Going man-to-wolf makes sense. We've all seen it, it's part of the human myth. Getting in touch with your wildside is not hard to imagine, it's almost romantic. It's what camping is all about. Becoming part of nature again. Nature can be a stand in for any number of animistic ideas. Getting in touch with the animal inside us, our spiritual nature, etc. <br /> <br /> But wolf-to-man is a concept that doesn't really feel real. You're a wolf, smart as far as animals go, but not capable of higher though or even certain complex emotions. Then bam, one day you can think more clearly and you have to somehow go about learning a language, which is incredibly, incredibly difficult to learn once you pass a certain age without being introduced to the concept, though I guess that can be hand-waived. Just like socializing a wolf is basically impossible past a certain age. It's basically just Encino Man. It's cool to be a true wolf, I guess, but that's basically it. You're not tapping into anything that's really resonant or potent. You're just a wolf in human-skin. I mean, being able to transform into a human doesn't give you anything to tap into except being able to use opposable thumbs and vocal chords. There aren't really any instincts that change how you behave or see the world, because humans are primarily conditioned through society, not instinct. Whatever survival instincts we have are already present in wolves except perhaps much quieter. The instinct to want to fit in maybe, is potent, but again ends up being a headache to deal with in roleplay. &quot;Wolf Wolf can't figure out what buttons to press on the elevator hururur. Look at how he holds the phone! Great roleplaying, Ben. This is a treat for everyone at the table.&quot; It just doesn't play out that way. I just think it's easier to play a werewolf close to his feral side than the actual wolf thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> In my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T19:57:57-07:00","id":849094,"title":"","content":"Don't like it, don't play it. Back on topic:<br /> <br /> Charlaquin mentionee earlier that greater ease of Reaching doesn't really fit the Urhanu. I agree: that's a WtA-ism, wolves being more spiritual than men. The Urhanu need something that speaks to a feral nature, not a spiritual nature. <br /> <br /> The Ulle'u, meanwhile, have a natural talent for shapeshifting. That makes sense: they did not spend an entire childhood locked in one physical form (or <i>any</i> physical form, for that matter); so changing forms should arguably come more naturally to them. Alternately, <i>they</i> should get the Reaching benefit, as the Shadow is something with which they're intimately familiar. I wouldn't give them both, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-17T20:05:10-07:00","id":849097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849094#post849094\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Don't like it, don't play it. Back on topic:<br /> The Ulle'u, meanwhile, have a natural talent for shapeshifting. That makes sense: they did not spend an entire childhood locked in one physical form (or <i>any</i> physical form, for that matter); so changing forms should arguably come more naturally to them. Alternately, <i>they</i> should get the Reaching benefit, as the Shadow is something with which they're intimately familiar. I wouldn't give them both, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you were to give them the Reaching benefit, I'd probably only apply it to crossing from Flesh to Shadow. Going the other way seems like it would be harder if anything, but I probably wouldn't give them a penalty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T01:51:25-07:00","id":849181,"title":"","content":"For Urhanu - maybe they easier come to Rage? Their instinct makes them more prone to the Fathers Wolff instincts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T09:30:16-07:00","id":849310,"title":"","content":"That would work if there was any sort of dice pool associated with Kuruth. As is, how could you represent that? More triggers? They'd need something in return too, to make it worthwhile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T10:39:13-07:00","id":849341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849034#post849034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alright, now the above is threadcrapping.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you honestly believe that, you and I need a talk about what threadcrapping is, but it's all good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T10:46:29-07:00","id":849345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849063#post849063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe. Probably.<br /> <br /> But I don't think anyone can deny Apocalypse was a blunt game, in ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>That it was..sometimes to an extent where the word &quot;blunt&quot; isn't enough to describe it. But back to how breeds could work for CoD.. it's more difficult to cleanly place, due to the overall murkiness of the Uratha's origin. Not saying it it's not a cool option to include for players who want it... I just see it as something as INCREDIBLY rare. So rare that the fact that one Predator King from the werewolf Night Horrors book is more or less a messiah- a wolf born Uratha just doesn't happen unless there is something REALLY big about to happen.. that or darker forces are at work XD. Either way, while it's a cool concept.. it just leaves a weird taste in my mouth is all. But people like what they like, I have no right to judge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T10:48:05-07:00","id":849346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849097#post849097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you were to give them the Reaching benefit, I'd probably only apply it to crossing from Flesh to Shadow. Going the other way seems like it would be harder if anything, but I probably wouldn't give them a penalty.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't that what it was stated the &quot;what if&quot; Urhanu did possess, a bonus for reaching when it came to merely crossing between Hisil or real world? I could be wrong of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T10:56:54-07:00","id":849349,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin was responding to a suggestion that the <i>Ulle'u</i> have an easier time Reaching, not the <i>Urhanu</i> \u2014 because wolves (Urhanu) are no more innately spiritual than men (Hishu) are, but these hypothetical spirit-born (Ulle'u) <i>would</i> be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T11:01:19-07:00","id":849351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849349#post849349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin was responding to a suggestion that the <i>Ulle'u</i> have an easier time Reaching, not the <i>Urhanu</i> \u2014 because wolves (Urhanu) are no more innately spiritual than men (Hishu) are, but these hypothetical spirit-born (Ulle'u) <i>would</i> be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dataweaver knows what's up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T11:41:55-07:00","id":849371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849349#post849349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Charlaquin was responding to a suggestion that the <i>Ulle'u</i> have an easier time Reaching, not the <i>Urhanu</i> \u2014 because wolves (Urhanu) are no more innately spiritual than men (Hishu) are, but these hypothetical spirit-born (Ulle'u) <i>would</i> be.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am completely aware. I was merely making an observation on what it was said with Urhanu, who do have an easier time of Reaching from what I remember.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T13:01:02-07:00","id":849408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849371#post849371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am completely aware. I was merely making an observation on what it was said with Urhanu, who do have an easier time of Reaching from what I remember.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the version Stu posted treats the Gauntlet as one step thinner for the purposes of Reaching. The thing is, why? It makes sense in Apocalypse for Lupus to have an easier time Stepping Sideways because in Apocalypse humans are disconnected from nature and by extension from the Umbra. But in Forsaken, it doesn't make sense. Wolves are no more spirits than humans are - if anything, humans are more connected to the Shadow because they collectively have a far greater influence on it than any other creature of flesh (save maybe werewolves). Why would werewolves born as wolves have an easier time Reaching than werewolves born as humans? On the other hand, if you decide to include a lineage of werewolves that are born as spirits, it would make perfect sense for them to be more connected with the Shadow than werewolves born of flesh, because that's where they're from. If it were me, I would probably give them a bonus for crossing <i>from</i> the Flesh <i>to</i> the Shadow because the Shadow is a more natural place for them to be. I would not give them that same bonus for crossing in the opposite direction because the Flesh is not a more natural place for them to be. I might even give them a penalty for crossing in that direction, but probably not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-18-2016, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:30:03-07:00","id":849527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849408#post849408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, the version Stu posted treats the Gauntlet as one step thinner for the purposes of Reaching. The thing is, why? It makes sense in Apocalypse for Lupus to have an easier time Stepping Sideways because in Apocalypse humans are disconnected from nature and by extension from the Umbra. But in Forsaken, it doesn't make sense. Wolves are no more spirits than humans are - if anything, humans are more connected to the Shadow because they collectively have a far greater influence on it than any other creature of flesh (save maybe werewolves). Why would werewolves born as wolves have an easier time Reaching than werewolves born as humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>The shortest answer I could give is Father Wolf was lord of the Border Marches, he had one paw in the shadow and physical worlds both. And as such, his wolf born descendants perhaps may have a closer connection to the gauntlet as a result, since they are wolves first thus they capture the symbolism that empowered Urfarah better than their human born kin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T17:44:19-07:00","id":849537,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849527#post849527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The shortest answer I could give is Father Wolf was lord of the Border Marches, he had one paw in the shadow and physical worlds both. And as such, his wolf born descendants perhaps may have a closer connection to the gauntlet as a result, since they are wolves first thus they capture the symbolism that empowered Urfarah better than their human born kin.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the implication there would be that an Urhanu is somehow more of a wolf than a human-born Uratha is. The whole reason I like the idea of Urhanu is to emphasize that Uratha aren't humans that can turn into wolves, they're shapeshifters that can take human form and wolf form Likewise, Urhanu should not be wolves that can turn into humans, they should be shapeshifters that can take wolf form and human form. Really the only difference should be which of those forms they were born in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-18-2016, 08:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T18:32:03-07:00","id":849561,"title":"","content":"I does makes sense for a wolf-born Uratha to have issues grasping abstract concepts like Math right after the first change, IMHO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T18:39:42-07:00","id":849563,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the perfect place for a Raised by Wolves Persistent Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T20:22:04-07:00","id":849585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849561#post849561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I does makes sense for a wolf-born Uratha to have issues grasping abstract concepts like Math right after the first change, IMHO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally. But if you want to play an Urhanu that doesn't struggle with those concepts, you can always just make a character that isn't fresh off the First Change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T21:13:31-07:00","id":849602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849537#post849537\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the implication there would be that an Urhanu is somehow more of a wolf than a human-born Uratha is. The whole reason I like the idea of Urhanu is to emphasize that Uratha aren't humans that can turn into wolves, they're shapeshifters that can take human form and wolf form Likewise, Urhanu should not be wolves that can turn into humans, they should be shapeshifters that can take wolf form and human form. Really the only difference should be which of those forms they were born in.</div> </div> </div> </div>For this concept of \u201cBreeds\u201d (which would be better named with some synonym for \u201cchildhood\u201d), you'd probably be best off keeping the supernatural distinctions to a minimum: everything should be attrubutable to Nurture rather than Nature.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T21:35:58-07:00","id":849605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849602#post849602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For this concept of \u201cBreeds\u201d (which would be better named with some synonym for \u201cchildhood\u201d), you'd probably be best off keeping the supernatural distinctions to a minimum: everything should be attrubutable to Nurture rather than Nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what I aim for, yeah.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T22:46:09-07:00","id":849616,"title":"","content":"OK; then it's a Youth, not a Breed. An Uratha with a Hishu Youth was born human and grew up human until the First Change; an Uratha with an Urhanu Youth was born a wolf and grew up a wolf until the First Change. <i>If</i> there is a third kind of Youth, it is one who came into being as a spirit and lived as a spirit until the First Change. <br /> <br /> With this in mind, I'm thinking that the Urhanu should get a free dot in Animal Ken, possibly with a free Specialty in Wolves (after all, you grew up <i>as</i> a wolf; comprehending how they think is second nature to you), along with the \u201cno Primary Mental Skills\u201d restriction and a Persistent Condition that replaces the -3 Unskilled penalty with automatic Chance Dice status until it's Resolved. Resolving this Condition involves spending enough Experiences to acclimate to human society, which should be <i>at least</i> as much as buying a Skill dot and maybe as much as buying an Attribute dot; I'm not sure which, but I'm leaning toward the latter. In the meantime, you're picking up Beats from this Condition whenever your outsider perspective causes you trouble, as per the normal rules for Conditions. <br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-19T07:14:21-07:00","id":849704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/840066-breeds-in-forsaken?p=849616#post849616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">OK; then it's a Youth, not a Breed. An Uratha with a Hishu Youth was born human and grew up human until the First Change; an Uratha with an Urhanu Youth was born a wolf and grew up a wolf until the First Change. <i>If</i> there is a third kind of Youth, it is one who came into being as a spirit and lived as a spirit until the First Change. <br /> <br /> With this in mind, I'm thinking that the Urhanu should get a free dot in Animal Ken, possibly with a free Specialty in Wolves (after all, you grew up <i>as</i> a wolf; comprehending how they think is second nature to you), along with the \u201cno Primary Mental Skills\u201d restriction and a Persistent Condition that replaces the -3 Unskilled penalty with automatic Chance Dice status until it's Resolved. Resolving this Condition involves spending enough Experiences to acclimate to human society, which should be <i>at least</i> as much as buying a Skill dot and maybe as much as buying an Attribute dot; I'm not sure which, but I'm leaning toward the latter. In the meantime, you're picking up Beats from this Condition whenever your outsider perspective causes you trouble, as per the normal rules for Conditions. <br /> <br /> How does that sound?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I like that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T10:31:28-07:00","id":851858,"title":"","content":"There's still the matter of pre-First Change Urhanu, and the wolf-equivalent of Wolf-Blooded humans. But at this point, I'll wait until <b>The Pack</b>, or at least a spoiler on wolves in the pack, comes out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}